# Bernstein–Vazirani recovering s = "101" (n = 3 input qubits + 1 ancilla).
# Oracle for f(x) = s · x mod 2 with s = 101 means: flip ancilla whenever
# x_0 ⊕ x_2 = 1, i.e. apply CNOT from each set bit of s into the ancilla.
